{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4456666","formula":"F₄N⁺","hill":"F4N","elements":["N","F"],"composition":{"F":4.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"Tetrafluoroammonium","ru":"Тетрафтораммоний"},"descriptions":{"en":"The tetrafluoroammonium cation (also known as perfluoroammonium) is a positively charged polyatomic ion with chemical formula NF+4. It is equivalent to the ammonium ion where the hydrogen atoms surrounding the central nitrogen atom have been replaced by fluorine. Tetrafluoroammonium ion is isoelectronic with tetrafluoromethane CF4, trifluoramine oxide ONF3, tetrafluoroborate BF−4 anion and the tetrafluoroberyllate BeF2−4 anion.","ru":"Тетрафтораммо́ний NF4+ — комплексный неорганический катион, представляющий собой аммоний, все четыре атома водорода в котором замещены фтором. Тетрафтораммоний является сильным окислителем и одним из немногих устойчивых соединений (и единственным бескислородным), в которых азот имеет степень окисления +5."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":5460510,"mass":90.0,"charge":1,"smiles":"[N+](F)(F)(F)F","inchikey":"LDOAUKNENSIPAZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"tetrafluoroazanium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5460510","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.266,"y":-0.207,"z":1.331,"el":"F"},{"x":-1.138,"y":0.758,"z":-0.127,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.183,"y":-1.21,"z":-0.624,"el":"F"},{"x":1.056,"y":0.659,"z":-0.58,"el":"F"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[1,4,1],[2,4,1],[3,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4456666","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetrafluoroammonium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%